[WorldCore Git Command Area]

Purpose:
This file stores safe Git command notes for WorldCore.

Repository:
WorldCore

Mode Notes:
Split Traffic mode may be active during some sessions.
When Split Traffic is active, do not push unless explicit permission is given.

Current Rule:
Push only when JacobS gives permission.

[Check Status]
Command:
git status

Use:
Shows changed, staged, untracked, and branch status.

[View Diff]
Command:
git diff

Use:
Shows exact local file changes before staging.

[View Diff Summary]
Command:
git diff --stat

Use:
Shows quick changed-file summary.

[Stage All Changes]
Command:
git add .

Use:
Stages all current local changes.

Warning:
Check for secrets and unrelated changes before using this.

[Stage One File]
Command:
git add path/to/file

Use:
Stages only one specific file.

[Commit Changes]
Command:
git commit -m "message here"

Use:
Creates a local commit.

Example:
git commit -m "Add Control Prime setup and traffic logs"

[Pull Latest Changes]
Command:
git pull

Use:
Pulls latest remote changes into the local repo.

Rule:
Run before pushing if the repo may have changed elsewhere.

[Push Changes]
Command:
git push

Use:
Pushes committed local changes to GitHub.

Permission Rule:
Only run when push permission is given.

[Full Safe Push Flow]
Commands:
git status
git diff --stat
git add path/to/file
git status
git commit -m "Add setup logs and device docs"
git pull
git push

Use:
Standard flow for checking, committing, pulling, and pushing selected files.

[Local Only Flow]
Commands:
git status
git diff --stat

Use:
Use during Split Traffic mode when pushing is not allowed.

[Safety Check Before Push]
Checklist:
- No `.kdbx` files
- No `.key` files
- No passwords
- No recovery codes
- No 2FA backup codes
- No sync/share codes
- No API tokens
- No GitHub tokens
- No private credential files
- No accidental vault backups
- Push permission confirmed

[Secret Search Commands]

PowerShell:
Select-String -Path (Get-ChildItem -Recurse -File).FullName -Pattern "password|token|secret|recovery|2FA|kdbx|key"

Git Bash:
grep -RniE "password|token|secret|recovery|2FA|kdbx|key" .

Use:
Searches the repo for risky words before pushing.

Warning:
These searches may find safe documentation that says not to store secrets.
Review results manually.

[Undo Staged Files]
Command:
git reset

Use:
Unstages files without deleting changes.

[Undo One File Before Commit]
Command:
git restore path/to/file

Use:
Restores one file back to the last committed version.

Warning:
This deletes local changes for that file.

[View Commit History]
Command:
git log --oneline --decorate --graph --all

Use:
Shows commit history in compact form.

[Branch Check]
Command:
git branch

Use:
Shows current branch.

[Remote Check]
Command:
git remote -v

Use:
Shows connected GitHub remote.

Notes:
WorldCore stores safe docs, logs, command notes, and project structure.
KeePassXC stores real secrets.
Do not place real vaults or credentials in this repo.

[Run KeepPass Helper GUI]
Command:
python KeepPass/App/keepass_helper.py

Use:
Launches the WorldCore KeepPass Helper GUI.

Safety:
The helper manages encrypted vault file movement only and does not read passwords.

[Run KeepPass Helper GUI Launcher]
Command:
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File KeepPass/App/Run_KeepPass_Helper.ps1

Use:
Finds a Python install with Tkinter/Tcl-Tk support and launches the WorldCore KeepPass Helper GUI.

Optional Python Path:
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File KeepPass/App/Run_KeepPass_Helper.ps1 -PythonPath C:/Path/To/Python/python.exe

Safety:
The launcher only checks Python Tkinter availability and starts the helper app.

[Python Add-on / Dependency Setup]

Commands:
python -m venv .venv
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install -r Requirements/requirements.txt
python -m tkinter
python KeepPass/App/keepass_helper.py
deactivate

Use:
Sets up the local Python add-on/plugin sandbox for WorldCore.

Safety:
Do not commit .venv.
Do not store secrets.
Do not pip install tkinter.
